    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_135e1f367346497c75f8cf77eb10c409143d4d6bc54937e8e9ad1b9ec8ec10ab",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source augments categorical Gram-block geometry with several numerical coordinates on rare local configurations: a nearby extremum of S(t) orders exception intensity, division by the natural local zero spacing makes a close-pair gap comparable across height, and large sampled values of Z(t) are located at joined occupancy patterns whose flanking gaps are measured in local Gram-interval lengths. Together these representations preserve information that a block-type label alone discards, without establishing that the coordinates are universally correlated.",
