    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1d74a11c58014cc9b4ad3599b789953e6ac04ad4668392d096af939ef63679f9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source supports a layered finite-verification architecture with a logical chain and a separate audit track. Error-bounded evaluations yield usable Gram-point signs; avoiding argument shifts preserves a fixed Gram-indexed census; adjacent machine-computed ranges and the inherited prefix supply continuous coverage; and five further Rosser-valid blocks precede application of the imported separation theorem. Targeted reruns and exact cross-machine agreement audit this chain without replacing its analytic obligations.",
