    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ba5e5bbd0cc84f63e8c70449a86ce96c48d1283a731faa2d3f2c3360ccacfa05",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The joint censuses support a two-level statistical description: the marginal abundance of block lengths and interval occupancies drifts with height, while type frequencies conditioned on a fixed block length appear to stabilize for adequately sampled lengths. This makes a length-indexed family of empirical type distributions a more faithful modeling target than pooling all blocks, and the source itself proposes an unknown discrete convex distribution depending on block length.",
